# 1. Initialize Git
git init

# 2. Add all files
git add .

# 3. Create your first commit
git commit -m "Initial commit: Industrial Conveyor App"

# 4. Set branch to main
git branch -M main

# 5. Link to your GitHub repo (REPLACE THE URL BELOW WITH YOURS)
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO_NAME.git

# 6. Push to GitHub
git push -u origin main


If you want to update later
Whenever you make changes, just run:

powershell
git add .
git commit -m "Update: added new feature"
git push
